taperness:
中：n. 细蜡烛, 烛芯；逐渐变弱；锥形物 (taper的变形)
英：n. The quality or state of being taper; tapering form;
   taper.

tegumentary:
中：[医] 体被的, 皮肤的
英：a. Of or pertaining to a tegument or teguments;
   consisting of teguments; serving as a tegument or covering.

temporo-auricular:
中：[医] 颞耳[部]的
英：a. Of or pertaining to both the temple and the ear;
   as, the temporo-auricular nerve.

thaumaturgical:
中：a. 奇术的, 魔术的
英：a. Of or pertaining to thaumaturgy; magical;
   wonderful.

thrivingness:
中：n. thriving的变形
英：n. The quality or condition of one who thrives;
   prosperity; growth; increase.

torpent:
中：[医] 迟钝的, 不活泼的; 缓和剂, 保护剂
英：a. Having no motion or activity; incapable of motion;
   benumbed; torpid.

towardliness:
中：n. towardly的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being towardly; docility;
   tractableness.

trichotomous:
中：[医] 三分的, 分三部的
英：a. Divided into three parts, or into threes;
   three-forked; as, a trichotomous stem.

typic:
音标：/'tipik/
中：[计] 典型的, 正规的
英：s being or serving as an illustration of a type;
